22. Short Project Explanation

AI Hand Gesture Computer Control System is a computer-vision application that uses a webcam to recognize hand gestures and convert them into computer actions. The system uses OpenCV for video capture, MediaPipe for hand landmark detection, and PyAutoGUI for controlling the mouse and keyboard. Different hand gestures are mapped to actions such as cursor movement, clicking, scrolling, and volume control. The project demonstrates a practical application of AI and computer vision for touch-free human-computer interaction.

23. Conclusion

The AI Hand Gesture Computer Control System demonstrates how computer vision and artificial intelligence can be used to create a natural and touch-free method of computer interaction. By detecting hand landmarks and recognizing predefined gestures, the system can perform various computer operations without requiring direct physical interaction with the mouse or keyboard.

The project can be further enhanced by adding more gestures, voice commands, media controls, presentation controls, and personalized gesture recognition.
